RK_COMMIT_SOURCERK_COMMIT_SCOPE- The scope names the area you changed, and reads as `area/subarea` where that is clearer. Prefer a scope this repository already uses, which `git log --format=%s | sed -n 's/^[a-z]*(\([^)]*\)).*/\1/p' | sort -u` lists. Coin a new scope only where no existing one names the area.
